      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The village’s first post office opened in July 1880 in Clayton Township, Genesee County, with Lennon as its inaugural postmaster.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lennon%2C_Michigan",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In February 1889 the post office moved to Shiawassee County, reflecting the village’s split between two townships.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lennon%2C_Michigan",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Peter Lennon also erected a grain elevator, sparking the growth of other businesses in the early community.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lennon%2C_Michigan",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Lennon sits along M‑13, straddling Venice Township in Shiawassee County to the west and Clayton Township in Genesee County to the east.",
